  "worked_solution": "First, since $s={t}^{2},$ we have that $t=\\sqrt{s}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\sqrt{s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\u27e8{(\\sqrt{s})}^{2},\\,-2{(\\sqrt{s})}^{2},\\,-2\u27e9 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\u27e8s,\\,-2s,\\,-2\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, since the curve is parameterized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-2s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-2)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\u27e81,\\,-2,\\,0\u27e9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
